      "text": "Cartagena"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:fb5db666cae6efb7",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "f77078a9b3eafe83df5ecbed226cda20464305bb2810e2ad26a3cafa2f28057f",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-worker-bde0f3741f24400e07188c41",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, set out on a sightseeing tour of Cartagena.\n\nYou'll see historic neighborhoods with colonial buildings and mansions lining cobbled streets, the modern tourist district of Bocagrande with its hotels and restaurants, and the Old Town enclosed by its defensive walls.\n\nThe tour takes you up La Popa Hill for panoramic views of Cartagena and its port. The Santa Cruz Convent stands at the top of the hill.\n\nYou'll then visit San Felipe de Barajas Castle, the city's largest fortification, which defended Cartagena against pirate attacks in the 18th century.\n\nYou can enter the Old Town through the Clock Tower. Within the walls are public squares, historic mansions and the Palace of the Inquisition with its ornate gateway.\n\nFor souvenirs, you can stop at the Las Bóvedas market, where you'll find small gifts, local handicrafts and hammocks.\n\nYou'll also see Plaza de la Aduana, the city's oldest square, which is home to City Hall and a statue of Columbus. Another stop is the Santa Clara Hotel, a former convent in the San Diego neighborhood.\n\nReturn to the hotel after the tour."
    },
